Day 3: Core Linux Navigation & File Operations

🎯 Focus & Objectives
Focused on fundamental Linux terminal commands, mastering absolute vs. relative pathing, and directory management.

🛠️ Key Commands & Concepts Covered
*Pathing Mechanics:** Understood the difference between Absolute (`/home/user/...`) and Relative (`../..`) pathing.
*Directory Navigation:** `pwd`, `ls -la` (including hidden files), and `cd`.
*File Operations:**
 Created files and directory structures with `touch` and `mkdir -p`.
 Managed assets using `cp -r` (recursive copy), `mv` (move/rename), and `rm -rf`.

💻 Practical Workflow Executed
```bash
#Set up working directory structure
mkdir -p ~/cyber_labs/day3 && cd ~/cyber_labs/day3

Manipulate files and directories
touch file1.txt file2.txt .hidden_config
mkdir backup
cp file1.txt backup/
mv file2.txt backup/renamed_file2.txt
